title "A Tour of tekx"
subtitle "Mathematics that means something"
author "Ada Lovelace"
date today

define block aside(title = "Aside")
  quote
    **{title}.** {body}

define golden as "the golden ratio"
define conjecture2 like theorem titled "Hypothesis"
define norm2(v) as ||v||_2 read as "the two-norm of {v}"

abstract
  This document is written in tekx. It shows how prose, structure and
  mathematics read naturally in source form, and how one source yields
  typeset pages, MathML, speech and clean copy text. // a comment

section Introduction #intro

Let us begin with {golden}, $phi = (1 + sqrt 5)/2$. It satisfies

    phi^2 = phi + 1 #golden

and appears in @fib. See also <https://example.org> and [the docs](https://example.org/docs).

theorem "Pythagoras" #pyth
  For a right triangle with legs $a$, $b$ and hypotenuse $c$,

      a^2 + b^2 = c^2

  holds.

proof
  Rearrange four copies of the triangle inside a square of side $a + b$.

aside "Note"
  Equation @golden defines *phi* up to sign.

